{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__Computer_Awareness__Computer__Computer_Awareness_-_Computer_-_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_39098_(20Q)","path":"organized/Others/Computer Awareness/Computer/Computer Awareness - Computer - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 39098 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"organized","category":"Others/Computer Awareness/Computer","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In the given figure, AD = 9cm, area of triangle ABC = 18&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup> and angle ABD = 60&deg;. If angle AED = 45&deg;, find the length of CE.</p><p><img width=272 height=148 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20728/image014.png\" ></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, AD = 9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; = 18&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; ABD = 60&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; AED = 45&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; CE &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=272 height=148 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20728/image014.png\" ></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9 - &radic;3 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9 - &radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9 - &radic;3/2 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9 - &radic;3/2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9 - 2&radic;3 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9 - 2&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9 - 3&radic;3 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9 - 3&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>As per the question,</p><p><img width=281 height=151 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20728/image015.png\" ></p><p>BD = 9/tan60&deg; = 9/&radic;3 cm = 3&radic;3 cm</p><p>Area of triangle = (Base  X  Height)/2</p><p>Base = BC = (2  X  18&radic;3)/9 = 4&radic;3 cm</p><p>DC = BC  -  BD = 4&radic;3  -  3&radic;3 = &radic;3 cm</p><p>As angle AED = 45&deg;, DE = AD = 9 cm</p><p>CE = DE  -  DC = 9 - &radic;3 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In right angled &#8710;GHJ, &#8736;H = 90&deg;. If area of triangle GHJ is 108 cm<sup>2</sup> and HJ(base) = 24 cm, then what is the approximate length of GJ?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#8710;GHJ &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;H = 90&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; GHJ &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 108 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; HJ(&#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;) = 24 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; GJ &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">29 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">29 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20.8 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20.8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25.6 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">22 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Area of triangle GHJ = 108 sq. cm</p><p>(1/2) x base x height = 108</p><p>(1/2) x HJ x GH = 108</p><p>(1/2) x 24 x GH = 108</p><p>GH = 9 cm</p><p>By Pythagoras theorem,</p><p>GJ = &radic;(24<sup>2</sup> + 9<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>GJ = &radic;657 = 25.6 cm (approx)</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In &#8710;KLM, &#8736;KLM = &#8736;KML = 60&deg; and P and Q are the points on sides KL and KM, respectively such that PQ || LM. If KP + MQ + LM = 36 cm and PQ = LM/2, then what is the perimeter (in cm) of the quadrilateral PQML?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#8710;KLM &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;KLM = &#8736;KML = 60&deg; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; KL &#2324;&#2352; KM &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367; PQ || LM &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; KP + MQ + LM = 36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; PQ = LM/2 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; PQML &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">45 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">45 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">27 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">54 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">54 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">63 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">63 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>In &#8710;KLM, &#8736;KLM = &#8736;KML = 60&deg;</p><p>Thus, &#8710;KLM is an equilateral triangle.</p><p>Let KL = LM = KM = 2x cm</p><p>Given PQ || LM and PQ = LM/2</p><p>So, P and Q are mid points of sides KL and KM, respectively.</p><p>Thus, KP = PL = KQ = QM = PQ = x cm</p><p>Now, KP + MQ + LM = 36</p><p>=&gt; x + x + 2x = 36</p><p>=&gt; 4x = 36</p><p>=&gt; x = 9 cm</p><p>Hence, perimeter of the quadrilateral PQML = PQ + QM + ML + LP = x + x + 2x + x = 5x = 5 * 9 = 45 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>O is the orthocentre of a triangle PQR, PO and RO are produced to meet QR and PQ at S and T respectively. If the bisectors of &#8736;OPR and &#8736;ORP meet at point U and &#8736;PQR is 68&deg;, then find the measure of &#8736;PUR.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>O &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; PQR &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2325;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, PO &#2324;&#2352; RO &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; S &#2324;&#2352; T &#2346;&#2352; QR &#2324;&#2352; PQ &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;OPR &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;ORP &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; U &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;PQR 68&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;PUR &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">152&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">152&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">146&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">146&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">164&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">164&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">140&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">140&deg;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=243 height=214 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p26261/image004.png\"></p><p>Since, O is the orthocentre of &#8710;PQR, </p><p>&#8736;POR = 180&deg; - &#8736;PQR</p><p>= 180&deg; - 68&deg;</p><p>= 112&deg;</p><p>&#8736;PUR = 90&deg; + 112&deg;/2</p><p>= 90&deg; + 56&deg;</p><p>= 146&deg;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the ratio between inradius and circumradius of a triangle is 3:7 respectively and the distance between incentre and circumcentre is 31.5 cm, then find the inradius of the triangle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2307;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 3:7 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2307;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 31.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2307;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">42.4 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">42.4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">13&radic;7 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">13&radic;7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10.5&radic;7 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10.5&radic;7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">13.5&radic;7 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">13.5&radic;7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let the inradius r = 3a cm</p><p>Circumradius R = 7a cm</p><p>Distance between incentre and circumcentre = 31.5 cm</p><p>&radic;(R<sup>2</sup>  -  2Rr) = 31.5</p><p>&radic;[(7a)<sup>2</sup>  -  (2*7a*3a)] = 31.5</p><p>&radic;(49a<sup>2</sup>  -  42a<sup>2</sup>) = 31.5</p><p>a&radic;7 = 31.5</p><p>a = 4.5&radic;7 cm</p><p>Hence, the inradius of the triangle = 3 * 4.5&radic;7 = 13.5&radic;7 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In the given figure, equilateral triangle ECB surmounts square ABCD. What is &ang;x?</p><p><img width=121 height=187 id=\"Picture 175\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p586/image003.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2351;&#2368; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ECB &#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; ABCD &#2325;&#2379; &#2328;&#2375;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310; &#2361;&#2376; | &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;x &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"121\" height=\"187\" id=\"Picture 175\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p586/image003.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">50&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50<sup>0</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">45&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">45<sup>0</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">35&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">35<sup>0</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">30&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30<sup>0</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>BC = CE, and BC = CD. Hence, CE = CD<p>&ang;CED = &ang;CDE (angles opposite to equal sides are equal)</p><p>&ang;C = 90 + 60 = 1500</p><p>&ang; CED = &ang;CDE = (180 - 150)/2 = 150</p><p>&ang;BEC = x + 150 = 600 </p><p>So, x = 45 &deg;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the perimeter and area of an isosceles triangle whose equal sides are 5 cm and the height is 4 cm.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; 5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; |</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">14 cm, 8 cm&#178;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, 8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16 cm, 12 cm&#178;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">17 cm, 14 cm&#178;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, 14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18 cm, 16 cm&#178;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, 16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Applying Pythagoras theorem,</p> <p>(Hypotenuse)&#178; = (Base)&#178; + (Height)&#178;</p> <p>=&gt; (5)&#178; = (0.5 x Base of isosceles triangle)&#178; + (4)&#178;</p> <p>=&gt; 0.5 x Base of isosceles triangle = 3</p> <p>=&gt; Base of isosceles triangle = 6 cm</p> <p>Therefore, perimeter = sum of all sides = 5 + 5 + 6 = 16 cm</p> <p>Area of triangle = 0.5 x Base x Height = 0.5 x 6 x 4 = 12 cm&#178;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In the given figure, &#8710;ABC is right angled at B. If AB = (X + 4) cm, BC = X/2 cm, AC = (X + 6) cm and the length of inradius of &#8710;ABC is 4 cm, then find the value of X.</p><p><img width=310 height=262 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15277/image011.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8710;ABC, B &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; AB = (X + 4) cm, BC = X/2 cm, AC = (X + 6) cm &#2324;&#2352; &#8710;ABC &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;:&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 4 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"310\" height=\"262\" id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15277/image011.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">18</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Given inradius (r) = 4 cm</p><p>Area of &#8710;ABC = 1/2 * (X/2) * (X + 4) = (X/4) * (X + 4) sq. cm</p><p>Semi-perimeter of &#8710;ABC = (X + 4 + X + 6 + (X/2))/2 = (5X + 20)/4 cm</p><p>We know that,</p><p>Inradius = Area/semi-perimeter</p><p>4 = (X<sup>2</sup> + 4X)/(5X + 20)</p><p>20X + 80 = X<sup>2</sup> + 4X</p><p>X<sup>2</sup>  -  16X  -  80 = 0</p><p>X<sup>2</sup>  -  20X + 4X  -  80 = 0</p><p>X(X  -  20) + 4(X  -  20) = 0</p><p>(X  -  20)(X + 4) = 0</p><p>X = 20.</p><p>Alternative solution:</p><p>In right angled triangle,</p><p>Inradius = (Perpendicular + Base  -  Hypotenuse)/2</p><p>4 * 2 = X + 4 + X/2  -  (X + 6)</p><p>16 = 2X + 8 + X  -  2X  -  12</p><p>X = 20</p><p></p><p>Shortcut Method:</p><p>As,  &#8710;ABC is right angled triangle.</p><p>So, By pythagoras theorem,</p><p>(x + 4)<sup>2</sup> + (x/2)<sup>2</sup> = (x + 6)<sup>2</sup></p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 16 + 8x + x<sup>2</sup>/4 = x<sup>2</sup> + 36 + 12x</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>/4 - 4x- 20 = 0</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> - 16 - 80 = 0</p><p>(x -20)(x + 4) = 0</p><p>so, x = 20</p><p></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a triangle ABC, AB = 8cm, &#8736; ABC = 30&#8304; and &#8736; ACB = 45&#8304;. Find area of the triangle ABC in cm<sup>2</sup>.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, AB = 8 cm, &#8736; ABC = 30&#8304; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736; ACB = 45&#8304; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; cm<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">8&radic;3 - 8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8&radic;3 - 8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8&radic;3 + 8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8&radic;3 + 8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4&radic;2 + 4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4&radic;2 + 4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4&radic;2 - 4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4&radic;2 - 4</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=200 height=218 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13643/image011.jpg\"></p><p>Let BC = x and AC = y.</p><p>Angle A = 180  -  angle B  -  angle C = 180  -  30&#8304; - 45&#8304; = 105&#8304;</p><p>Area of triangle = 1/2 *8*x*sin30&#8304; = 1/2 *x*y*sin45&#8304;</p><p>4 = y/&radic;2</p><p>y = 4&radic;2 cm</p><p>Area = 1/2 *8*4&radic;2 * sin105&#8304; = 16&radic;2*sin75&#8304; (sin105&#8304; = sin75&#8304;)</p><p>= 16&radic;2 * (&radic;3 + 1)/2&radic;2 = 8(&radic;3 + 1) cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Note: sin 75&#8304; = (&radic;3 + 1)/2&radic;2 or sin75&#8304; = sin(45&#8304; + 30&#8304;), calculate the value by formula sin(A+B).</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Angle bisector of &#8736;Q in &#8710;PQR is QS that meets PR at point S. If PQ = (x + 1) cm, QR = (2x  -  1) cm, PS = (x  -  2) cm and RS = (x + 2) cm, then find the length of side PR.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#8710;PQR&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;Q &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; QS &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; S &#2346;&#2352; PR &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; PQ = (x + 1) &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, QR = (2x - 1) &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, PS = (x - 2) &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; RS = (x + 2) &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; PR &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">12 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=196 height=187 id=\"Picture 82\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11857/image014.png\"></p><p>PQ = x + 1</p><p>QR = 2x  -  1</p><p>PS = x  -  2</p><p>RS = x + 2</p><p><b>We know that: </b>In the above figure, QS is the angle bisector, then- QP: PS = QR: RS</p><p>(x + 1): (x  -  2) = (2x  -  1): (x + 2)</p><p>(x + 1) (x + 2) = (x  -  2) (2x  -  1)</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 3x + 2 = 2x<sup>2</sup>  -  5x + 2</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> = 8x</p><p>x = 8</p><p>PR = PS + RS</p><p>= (x  -  2) + (x + 2)</p><p>= 2x = 16 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a &#8710;ABC, the respective ratio between the sides AB, BC and CA is 4: 5: 2. The perimeter of &#8710;ABC is 44 cm. If D and E are mid- points of AB and AC respectively, then the area of an equilateral triangle whose side is equal to the length of DE is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#8710;ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, AB, BC &#2324;&#2352; CA &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4: 5: 2 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#8710;ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 44 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; D &#2324;&#2352; E &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; AB &#2324;&#2352; AC &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;-&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; DE &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">25&radic;3 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25&radic;3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">50 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5&radic;3 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5&radic;3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let the length of AB, BC and CA be 4Y cm, 5Y cm and 2Y cm respectively.</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>(4Y + 5Y + 2Y) = 44</p><p>11Y = 44</p><p>Y = 4</p><p>Therefore, length of AB, BC and CA are 16 cm, 20 cm and 8 cm respectively.</p><p>Given, D and E are mid-points of AB and AC respectively. So, the length of DE will be half of the length of BC.</p><p>So, DE = 20/2 = 10 cm</p><p>Area of equilateral triangle = &radic;3/4 * (side)<sup>2</sup> = &radic;3/4 * 10<sup>2</sup> = 25&radic;3 sq. cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>&#8710;ABC are &#8710;QPR are similar and AB = 12 cm, AC = 9 cm, PQ = 8 cm, and QR = 6 cm. Length of median BD is 10 cm, then find the length of corresponding median in &#8710;PQR.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#8710;ABC &#8710;QPR &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; AB = 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, AC = 9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, PQ = 8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; QR = 6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8710;PQR &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">10/3 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10/3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20/3 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20/3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">55/6 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">55/6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7.5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=288 height=154 id=\"Picture 76\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11857/image012.png\"></p><p>Since &#8710;ABC ~ &#8710;QPR:</p><p>AB: PQ = AC: QR = BD: PS</p><p>12: 8 = 10: PS</p><p>PS = 20/3 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In &#916;ABC points P, Q, and R are taken on AB, BC and CA, respectively, such that BQ = PQ and QC = QR. If &ang;BAC = 75&deg;, what is the measure of &ang;PQR(in degrees)?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#916;ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; AB, BC &#2324;&#2352; CA &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;: &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; P, Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; BQ = PQ &#2324;&#2352; QC = QR &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;BAC = 75&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;PQR (&#2337;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">40</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">30</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">50</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">75</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">75</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=206 height=218 id=\"Picture 54\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19955/image044.png\"></p><p>&#8736;BAC = 75&deg;</p><p>Let, &#8736;ABC = x&deg; and &#8736;ACB = y&deg;</p><p>&#8736;ABC = &#8736;PBQ = &#8736;QPB = x&deg; [Given: BQ = PQ]</p><p>&#8736;ACB = &#8736;RCQ = &#8736;QRC = y&deg; [Given: QC = QR]</p><p>In &#916;ABC:</p><p>&#8736;ABC + &#8736;ACB + &#8736;BAC = 180&deg;</p><p>x + y + 75&deg; = 180&deg;</p><p>x + y = 105&deg; ........ (1)</p><p>In, &#916;BPQ:</p><p>&#8736;PBQ + &#8736;QPB + &#8736;PQB = 180&deg;</p><p>x + x + &#8736;PQB = 180&deg;</p><p>2x +&#8736;PQB = 180&deg; ........ (2)</p><p>In, &#916;CRQ:</p><p>&#8736;RCQ + &#8736;QRC + &#8736;RQC = 180&deg;</p><p>y + y + &#8736;RQC = 180&deg;</p><p>2y + &#8736;RQC = 180&deg; ........ (3)</p><p>From (1), (2), and (3):</p><p>(2x + &#8736;PQB) + (2y + &#8736;RQC)  -  2 (x + y) = 180&deg; + 180&deg; - 2 * 105&deg;</p><p>&#8736;PQB+ &#8736;RQC= 150&deg;</p><p>&#8736;PQB + &#8736;RQC + &#8736;PQR = 180&deg;</p><p>150&deg; + &#8736;PQR = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;PQR = 30&deg;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In &#8710;GHJ, HJ is parallel to KL and GK: KH = 3: 11 and GL = 27 cm. What is the difference between the length of LJ and GL?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#8710;GHJ &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; HJ, KL &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; GK: KH = 3: 11 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; GL = 27 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; LJ &#2324;&#2352; GL &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">54 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">54 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">33 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">33 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">72 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=209 height=206 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19361/image010.jpg\"></p><p>In &#8710;GKL and &#8710;GHJ, we have,</p><p>HJ is parallel to KL, therefore -</p><p>&#8736;GKL = &#8736;GHJ</p><p>&#8736;GLK = &#8736;GJH</p><p>And &#8736;KGL = &#8736;HGJ (common angle)</p><p>Thus, &#8710;GKL and &#8710;GHJ are similar triangles.</p><p>So, applying similar triangle property.</p><p>GK/GH = GL/GJ = KL/HJ</p><p>3/14 = 27/(27 + LJ)</p><p>=&gt; 81 + 3 LJ = 14 * 27</p><p>=&gt; LJ = 297/3</p><p>=&gt; LJ = 99</p><p>So, difference = 99 - 27 = 72 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In the following figure, the internal bisectors of &#8736;ABC and &#8736;ACB meet at D and internal bisectors of &#8736;DBC and &#8736;DCB meet at E. If &#8736;BAC = 100&deg;, find the value of (&#8736;BEC  -  &#8736;BDC)/2.</p><p><img width=333 height=229 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15383/image048.jpg\" ></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;ABC &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;ACB &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; D &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;DBC &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;DCB &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; E &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;BAC = 100&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (&#8736;BEC - &#8736;BDC)/2 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"333\" height=\"229\" id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15383/image048.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">20&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8&deg;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Given &#8736;BAC = 100&deg;</p><p>The internal bisectors of &#8736;ABC and &#8736;ACB meet at D and internal bisectors of &#8736;DBC and &#8736;DCB meet at E.</p><p>So, D is the incenter of &#8710;ABC and E is the incenter of &#8710;BDC.</p><p>&#8736;BDC = 90 + (&#8736;BAC)/2 = 90 + (100/2) = 140&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BEC = 90 + (&#8736;BDC)/2 = 90 + (140/2) = 160&deg;</p><p>So, value of (&#8736;BEC  -  &#8736;BDC)/2 = (160  -  140)/2 = 20/2 = 10&deg;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a right angled triangle PQR which is right angles at Q, S is the bisector of &#8736;P such that &#8736;PSR = 117&#730; and S lies on QR, then what is the measure of &#8736;R?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; PQR &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2379; Q &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;, S, &#8736;P &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; &#2311;&#2360; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#8736;PSR = 117&#730; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; S, QR &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;R &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">36&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36&#730;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">42&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">42&#730;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">48&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">48&#730;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">52&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">52&#730;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=202 height=208 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8336/image002.png\"></p><p>Here, &#8736;PSR = 117&#730;</p><p>Then, &#8736;PSQ = 180  -  117 = 63&#730;</p><p>Now, &#8736;QPS = &#8736;SPR = 180  -  90  -  63 = 27&#730;</p><p>Therefore, &#8736;R = 180  -  2 * 27  -  90 = <b>36</b><b>&#730;</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In the following figure, find the value of &#8736;BAC - &#8736;ABC.</p><p><img width=363 height=221 id=\"Picture 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3789/image014.png\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;BAC - &#8736;ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"363\" height=\"221\" id=\"Picture 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3789/image014.png\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">55&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">55<sup>0</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">35&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">35<sup>0</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">45&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">45<sup>0</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">65&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">65<sup>0</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>&#8736;EDA = 90<sup>0 </sup>- 20<sup>0</sup></p><p>=&gt; &#8736;EDA = 70<sup>0</sup></p><p>&#8736;AED + &#8736;EDA + &#8736;EAD = 180<sup>0</sup> [Sum of interior angles of a triangle = 180<sup>0</sup>]</p><p>=&gt; 55<sup>0</sup> + 70<sup>0</sup> + &#8736;EAD = 180<sup>0</sup></p><p>=&gt; 125<sup>0</sup> + &#8736;EAD = 180<sup>0</sup></p><p>=&gt; &#8736;EAD = 180<sup>0</sup> - 125<sup>0</sup></p><p>=&gt; &#8736;EAD = 55<sup>0</sup></p><p>&#8736;BAC = &#8736;EAD + &#8736;DAC</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;BAC = 55<sup>0</sup> + 15<sup>0</sup></p><p>=&gt; &#8736;BAC = 70<sup>0</sup></p><p>Now,</p><p>&#8736;BED + &#8736;AED = 180<sup>0</sup> [Linear pair]</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;BED + 55<sup>0</sup> = 180<sup>0</sup></p><p>=&gt; &#8736;BED = 180<sup>0</sup> - 55<sup>0</sup></p><p>=&gt; &#8736;BED = 125<sup>0</sup></p><p>&#8736;BED + &#8736;EDB + &#8736;DBE = 180<sup>0</sup> [Sum of interior angles of a triangle = 180<sup>0</sup>]</p><p>=&gt; 125<sup>0</sup> + 20<sup>0</sup> + &#8736;DBE = 180<sup>0</sup></p><p>=&gt; 145<sup>0</sup> + &#8736;DBE = 180<sup>0</sup></p><p>=&gt; &#8736;DBE = 180<sup>0</sup> - 145<sup>0</sup></p><p><b>=</b>&gt; &#8736;DBE = 35<sup>0</sup></p><p>&#8736;BAC - &#8736;ABC = 70<sup>0 </sup> -  35<sup>0 </sup>= 35<sup>0</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>&#8710;STU is right-angled at T. Points V and W are on side ST such that SV: VW: WT = 1: 2: 3 respectively. Points X and Y are on side SU such that VX || WY || TU. If length of side TU is 48 cm, then what is (VX + WY) equal to?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#8710;STU, &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; T &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; V &#2324;&#2352; W &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; ST &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; SV: VW: WT = 1: 2: 3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; SU &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; VX || WY || TU &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; TU &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 48 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (VX + WY) &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">32 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">48 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">48 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><img width=267 height=265 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18894/image016.jpg\"></p><p>SV: VW: WT = 1: 2: 3</p><p>Let SV = a cm, VW = 2a cm, and WT = 3a cm</p><p>&#8710;SVX, &#8710;SWY, and &#8710;STU are similar triangles. </p><p>In &#8710;SVX and &#8710;STU, </p><p>VX/TU = SV/ST</p><p>VX = 48 * a/(a + 2a + 3a) = 8 cm</p><p>Now in &#8710;SWY, and &#8710;STU, </p><p>WY/TU = SW/ST</p><p>=&gt; WY = 48 * (a + 2a)/(a + 2a + 3a) = 24 cm</p><p>Hence, VX + WY = 8 + 24 = 32 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>&#8710;MNO is a right-angle triangle with &#8736;M = 90&deg;. If length of the side MN of the triangle is 16 cm and area of &#8710;MNO 96 cm<sup>2</sup> then ON =?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#8710;MNO &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8736;M = 90&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; MN &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#8710;MNO &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 96 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; ON =?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">32 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">30 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>According to the question,</p><p><img width=217 height=140 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/er230518ber1img001.png\"></p><p>Given that, length of the side MN of the triangle is 16 cm and area of &#8710;MNO is 96 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Area of &#8710;MNO = (1/2) x b x h</p><p>96 = (1/2) x 16 x h</p><p>H = 12 cm</p><p>According to Pythagoras theorm</p><p>ON<sup>2</sup> = OM<sup>2</sup> + MN<sup>2</sup></p><p>ON<sup>2</sup> = 144 + 256</p><p>ON = 20 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>&#8710;ABC has &#8736;A = 70&deg;, &#8736;B = 80&deg;. D is the incentre of &#8710;ABC. DM is perpendicular to BC and DP is the angle bisector of &#8736;BDC. Find &#8736;PDM.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#8710;ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8736;A = 70<sup>0</sup>, &#8736;B = 80<sup>0</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; D, &#8710;ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2307;&#2325;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; DM, BC &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; DP, &#8736;BDC &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#8736;PDM &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">25&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25<sup>0</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12.5&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12.5<sup>0</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15<sup>0</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7.5&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7.5<sup>0</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=297 height=148 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14580/image005.png\"> </p><p><img width=201 height=147 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14580/image006.png\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}